                  :protocol ["Under future separately scoped authority, verify the exact S2A context, create fresh fixture root, and establish the real validated initial head through read-head!. A digest is byte identity, not authorization." "Construct catalog-valid event from the independently qualified cut; retain exact proposed event identity/bytes, revision and predecessor. Call append! with the exact expected head; classify returned owner result only according to independently inspected pinned S2A/Clio semantics, then read and validate actual head and replay complete owner history. Bind exact event, predecessor, resulting head, causal links and revision to retained owner evidence; if API evidence cannot establish a fact, leave it unknown and stop." "Treat timeout, thrown error, mismatched evidence, or uncertain admission as unresolved. Retain exact pending identity and predecessor; do not submit a competing event, assume rejection, or synthesize a trusted ACK. Resolve using authorized owner read/replay evidence; late acceptance updates historical accounting only, never revives a lease." "On proven coverage loss after baseline admission, revoke fixture eligibility immediately; append and independently prove exactly one causally valid gap at the old revision. Only after that gap is admitted may a new independently justified cut be appended as a directly causal higher-revision reconciliation with fresh incarnations. Unknown gap status blocks reconciliation. History retains the gap."]
                  :limitations "This tests private S2A/Clio fixture append and replay alongside native observation. It does not authenticate P1, add a product-level bridge, establish real-world freshness or override the workspace provenance rule. If the narrowly scoped fixture root/append conflicts with an applicable rule, execution requires explicit scoped adjudication first."}
 :assumptions {:A1-isolation "Future independently verified sandbox/namespace or equivalent prevents access to operator sockets/files and same-UID outside processes; owned X server and i3 are the only addressable targets."
               :A2-completion "Each permitted X/i3 operation has an independently justified completion witness; neither sleeps, an i3 SEND_TICK reply, tree silence nor client request submission alone proves X processing. If proof is unavailable, no positive cut."
               :A3-exclusion "An independently enforced and evidenced no-writer interval begins after A2 and spans both trees and post marker. Account for all fixture clients, WM internal activity, asynchronous X requests and any possible autonomous mutation; stop if exclusion cannot be established."
               :A4-stream "Exact installed-build ordering for subscribed events and matching tick on a single intact FIFO connection is documented and separately qualified; frame integrity, subscription, sequence, generation, counters and nonce uniqueness are witnessed. Proxy disruption fails qualification."
               :A5-identity "Each producer, XID, epoch, incarnation and workspace identity is independently bound to fixture ownership; unknown, duplicate, unowned or ambiguous identities fail."
               :A6-field-coverage "The descriptor enumerates supported native fields and operations, event classes and whether exact distro source plus patches and controlled probes establish notification coverage. A missing notification path is not cured by ticks; rely only on independently proven A2/A3 for the narrowly declared quiescent fixture, or stop."
               :outcome "Only a supported synthetic-owned fixture subset at the stated cut under proven applicable assumptions; no general i3, arbitrary workload, continuous-currentness, operator desktop or S2B completion claim."}
 :stream-and-oracle {:preflight "Subscribe on one serialized event connection to every event class required for declared supported fields; verify success and consume initial first=true tick without using it as a fence. Start fresh generation; record bounded frames, monotonic sequence, queue/drop counts, epoch and ownership. Unsupported events or message paths fail closed unless explicitly classified irrelevant by reviewed descriptor; malformed, unknown, oversized or unaccounted frames revoke coverage."
                     :sequence ["After all controlled mutations, establish A2 and enter evidenced A3 no-writer interval. Send unique unpredictable pre nonce; wait for matching first=false tick event on event stream. Its SEND_TICK reply is not a fence." "After consuming pre marker, request collector-side GET_TREE and parse its complete bounded response; separately request oracle GET_TREE and independently parse/traverse nodes and floating_nodes. Both requests and completed responses must occur within the same uninterrupted A3 interval and the same pre/post generation and epoch. The oracle shares only frozen schema and explicitly assigned owned fixture identities, never parsing, mapping or normalization implementation." "Send distinct post nonce after both responses; consume its matching first=false event on the same intact stream. Only now close cut eligibility, provided no relevant event appeared between markers, no loss/overflow/unknown message occurred, A2/A3 remain proven through post, and all identity and supported-field assertions pass. Record request/reply and stream indices, monotonic times, marker nonces, counters, isolation and exclusion witnesses. The SEND_TICK reply is never the fence." "Compare exact normalized [epoch XID incarnation workspace-UUID] sets against the independently replayed admitted owner subset for that same qualified candidate; independently assert only declared supported hierarchy/floating/move/resize facts from bounded tree and fixed stimulus. Ownership, duplicate and schema mismatches deny; do not claim full-tree or geometry equality from subset equality. Record sanitized synthetic-only evidence sufficient to audit both traversals and mapping."]
                     :proxy-cases [{:case :event-before-pre :schedule "Server-generates E before PRE; FIFO release E then PRE. E is consumed before PRE and may be incorporated by subsequent trees only if A2/A3 and coverage are proven; it does not automatically invalidate the later cut."} {:case :held-across-pre :schedule "Server-generates E before PRE but proxy attempts to deliver PRE before E. This violates qualified FIFO or reflects loss; invalidate transport qualification, never describe as native ordering."} {:case :within-cut :schedule "Server-generates relevant E after PRE and before POST; deliver in FIFO between markers. Reject candidate irrespective of eventual tree equality."} {:case :held-past-post :schedule "Proxy holds a pre-POST event across delivered POST, drops bytes, or reorders frames. Invalidate transport qualification and cut; record proxy fault, not native behavior."}]
                     :faults "Explicitly test subscription failure; missing, wrong, initial, duplicate or reused nonce; reply without matching event; generation drift; request socket surviving event-stream loss; queue overflow; partial/oversized/malformed/unsupported frames; parser divergence; identity mismatch; timeout and churn. Deny or invalidate as specified; preserve no-success evidence."}
 :lifetime-and-matrix {:positive "At least two owned xmessage windows, two fixture workspaces, nested split and floating; fixed scoped stimulus and verified X/i3 completion, A1-A6, two independently parsed trees, exact real S2A owner append and replay subset. Every supported field and operation has a named evidence/coverage row."
                       :loss "Close/overflow event channel while request channel may survive; revoke eligibility, retain pending owner event on ambiguous outcome, resolve exact admitted head before any competing append, prove one old-revision gap and direct higher-revision reconciliation; retain historical gap and assert stale callbacks cannot restore eligibility."
                       :identity "Record X-server epoch and verified producer ownership plus distinct incarnation UUID per window lifetime. Close denies old target; same-epoch numeric XID reuse requires new incarnation. Cross-epoch numeric equality never implies identity. On uncertain reconnect, retire prior incarnation and target even if numeric XID remains; deny historical membership migration and require fresh justified identity. Verify negative stale target and replay membership assertions."
                       :reuse "Attempt actual same-epoch and cross-epoch XID reuse only within separately permitted owned fixture. If infeasible, explicitly retain native reuse as missing coverage; separately permitted offline deterministic collision schedules are not native proof."
                       :negative "Exercise parser and identity divergence, unsupported native fields/messages, event loss, gap rejection/unknown, late acceptance, no completion witness, failed exclusion and budget exhaustion. No fixture qualification on any unresolved necessary evidence."}
